{"id": "q0072", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 171000483, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 5, "query": "Timothy has three times the number of pens that George owns. Sarah has half as many pens as Timothy. If George has 18 pens, how many pens does Sarah have?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0072.wav", "input_sha256": "52df4602799567f8ef08e13b7e1438b895224e3197853c77ab4d09a0a4d3e5f3", "input_samples": 196000, "input_s": 12.25, "n_real_chunks": 13, "score": 0.0526, "act": 0.9985, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Okay, so if George has 18 pens, then Timothy has three times that amount. So let's do the math: 3 times 18 is 54. So Timothy has 5 4 pens. Sarah has half as many pens as Timot hy, so we divide 54 by 2, which gives us 27. Therefore, Sarah has 27 pens.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 12, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 16, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0072_local_local.wav", "sha256": "1ae623cb0c55c267afc6928c239ee95b0b92d62bdc367211910dcda9706f08c8", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 16.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.056, 1.103, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.058, 2.103, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.058, 3.102, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.06, 4.107, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.058, 5.104, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.058, 6.106, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.062, 7.11, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.085, 8.