{"id": "q0239", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 4195060289, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 5, "query": "A steel cylinder contains liquid at a mean bulk temperature of 80°F. Steam condensing at 212°F on the outside surface is used for heating the liquid. The coefficient of heat transfer on the steam side is 1,000 Btu/hr-ft^2-°F. The liquid is agitated by the stirring action of a turbine impeller. Its diameter is 2 ft., and it moves at an angular velocity of 100 rpm. The cylinder is 6 ft. long, with a diameter of 6 ft. and a wall thickness of 1/8 in. The thermal conductivity of steel may be taken as 9.4 Btu/hr-ft^2-°F. Properties of the liquid, taken as constant, are: c_p = 0.6 Btu/lbm-°Fk = 0.1 Btu/hr-ft-°F \\rho = 60lbm/ft^3 The viscosity at 130°F is 653.4lbm/ft-hr, and at 212°F is 113.74lbm/ft-hr. Calculate the time required to raise the mean bulk temperature of the liquid to 180°F.\n\nA. 3.5 hr\nB. 1.92 hr\nC. 4.0 hr\nD. 1.75 hr\nE. 2.0 hr\nF. 3.0 hr\nG. 2.5 hr\nH. 1.5 hr\nI. 2.75 hr\nJ. 2.15 hr\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0239.wav", "input_sha256": "a7916738f88aa001428acbe4e6886ab0f668c7c6710cd354dbc08037fe1e4293", "input_samples": 1138200, "input_s": 71.138, "n_real_chunks": 72, "score": 0.9633, "act": 0.9995, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "The correct answer is E, 2. 05 hours.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 71, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak